# Local Model Routing (Ollama)

Bulk, low-stakes text work runs via **local scripts**, not in-agent prose generation. Full guide: [local-model-integration.md](../../project-docs/reference/local-model-integration.md).

## When to delegate (run terminal CLI)

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| Check Ollama | `uv run python3 scripts/local_llm_cli.py health` |
| Edge hints | `build_hints.py --llm-ideas-cmd "uv run python3 scripts/local_llm_cli.py edge-hints"` |
| Prompt retro draft | `local_llm_cli.py retro-draft --evidence FILE --task-family SLUG` → review → save retro |
| Commit message only | `local_llm_cli.py commit-message` → user runs `git commit` |
| Weekly distill + LLM | `distill_prompt_learnings.py --enable-llm` → review digest section only |

After local CLI output: **verify** before writing state files. Do not auto-commit.

## Never use local model for

- Multi-file code edits, MCP (Robinhood), pytest fix loops
- Deep/update research synthesis
- Trading, thesis writes, portfolio decisions
- Autonomous git commit/push/PR
- Skill improvement/generation PR pipelines

Stay on Cursor subscription agent for those tasks.

## Graceful skip

If `health` exits 2, warn user and either skip the LLM step or ask before using Cursor tokens.
